Documentation Typically Required Before Placement
Startups
Tines — Before beginning a placement at Tines, students would typically be required to sign a Non-Disclosure Agreement (NDA) given the sensitive nature of the automation workflows and client data the company handles. A placement learning agreement between the student, their institution, and Tines would also be expected, along with proof of any relevant academic standing required by the college.
Solidroad — Due to Solidroad's use of AI and personal data in its simulation platform, students may be required to sign data handling agreements in addition to a standard NDA. A placement contract outlining the student's role, responsibilities, and duration would typically be completed before starting, alongside any institutional documentation required by their college.
SMEs
Workvivo — Given the volume of employee data Workvivo manages on behalf of clients, students would likely be required to sign confidentiality agreements and data processing acknowledgements before commencing placement. Standard documentation such as a placement learning agreement, emergency contact forms, and proof of insurance or institutional cover would also be expected.
Phorest — Students joining Phorest would typically need to sign an NDA due to the sensitive client and business data they may encounter. A formal placement agreement between the company and the educational institution would be required, along with any health and safety induction forms and confirmation of GDPR awareness training completed prior to starting.
Multinationals
Google — Placement at Google involves an extensive pre-start documentation process. Students would be expected to complete a formal offer and contract, sign comprehensive confidentiality and intellectual property agreements, and complete mandatory compliance training before their first day. Background checks may also be required depending on the role and jurisdiction.
Stripe — As a regulated financial technology company, Stripe may require students to undergo background screening in addition to signing NDAs and data protection agreements. A formal internship contract outlining compensation, role scope, and confidentiality obligations would be standard, along with any institutional placement agreements and proof of eligibility to work.
